  "market_commentary": {
    "overview": "",
    "bulkers": "The Baltic Dry Index closed today at 3,224 points, rising from 2,991 points recorded last Friday.  \n \nOne might expect the sale-and-purchase market to ease ahead of Posidonia 2026, which start next week \nfrom June 1 to 5. Yet there's no sign of a \"Posidonia lull\" so far as activity stayed strong the past week, \ndespite slight fluctuations in the freight market.  \n \nWe recorded an impressive 24 dry-bulk transactions this week - four more than last week: 3 x capes, 2 \nx post- panamaxes, 1 x kamsarmax, 5 x panamaxes, 4 x ultramaxes, 5 x supramaxes and 4 x \nhandysizes, as asset prices continue to show remarkable resilience, maintaining multi-year highs.",
    "demolition": "The Subcontinent markets remain stable with minimal activity. For an overview of \ndemolition market rates, please check our comprehensive demometer below:"
  },
